    "introduction": "Next sells clothing, homeware and beauty products through stores and online channels, combining its own ranges with third-party brands. Its operations also include consumer credit and Total Platform services that provide capabilities such as websites, warehousing and distribution to other retailers. Revenue therefore comes from merchandise sales and additional commercial services. Its online infrastructure allows the group to reach customers beyond its physical stores and support partner brands. Product selection, inventory discipline and fulfilment efficiency are central to the model. Consumer spending and fashion demand influence sales, while the balance between stores, digital retail and platform services affects how the business develops.",
